on rate with systematic differences by league) further undermines generalizability", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["selection bias", "exclusion rate"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [16, 17]}, {"id": 19, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[20, 22]], "note": "section separator"}, {"id": 20, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[23, 24]], "note": "section 1 heading"}, {"id": 21, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[25, 25]], "note": "Main Result subheading"}, {"id": 22, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[26, 30]], "assertion": "the primary adjusted risk difference result was 0.171pp, 95% CI [-0.022,0.363], SE 0.098pp, p=0.082, not significant at α=0.05", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["adjusted risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 23, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[31, 31]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 24, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[32, 32]], "note": "Interpretation subheading"}, {"id": 25, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[33, 33]], "assertion": "the model adjusted for position, league country, games, yellow cards per game, age, height and weight", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["position", "league country", "games", "yellow cards per game", "age", "height", "weight"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [26, 27]}, {"id": 26, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[33, 33]], "assertion": "dark-skinned players had a 0.17 percentage point higher probability of receiving a red card than light-skinned players", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["dark-skinned players", "light-skinned players"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [25, 27]}, {"id": 27, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[33, 33]], "assertion": "the effect is small in absolute terms against a 1.26% baseline, a relative increase of about 14%", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["baseline red card rate"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [25, 26]}, {"id": 28, "kind": "